CREATE INDEX ON products USING gin (attrs jsonb_path_ops);

SELECT * FROM products WHERE attrs @> '{"color":"red"}';
```

**Not an entity-attribute-value table** — EAV needs a self-join per attribute and loses types. `jsonb` with a GIN index keeps the containment query to one index scan.

```sql
CREATE TABLE readings (id bigint, ts timestamptz NOT NULL, ...)
  PARTITION BY RANGE (ts);
CREATE TABLE events_2026_04 PARTITION OF readings
  FOR VALUES FROM ('2026-04-01') TO ('2026-05-01');
CREATE INDEX ON readings USING brin (ts);
```

**Not moving to a different database, or sharding in the application** — range partitioning prunes whole partitions at plan time and turns retention into `DROP TABLE` instead of a long `DELETE`. BRIN suits naturally-ordered timestamps at a fraction of a b-tree's size.

